*   `static/`: (If present, standard for Hugo) For static files that are copied directly to the public directory without processing.
*   `layouts/`: Project-level layout overrides or new layouts.
*   `archetypes/`: Project-level content archetypes.
*   `i18n/`: Project-level translation files (e.g., `en.toml`, `de.toml`).
*   `data/`: Data files (JSON, YAML, TOML) that can be used in templates.
*   `public/`: Output directory where the generated static site is placed after running `hugo`. (Typically gitignored)
